From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aayush Nair <aayushnair204@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:00:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Documentation: Describe how Kairos task classes steer timer
 slack

Describe CONFIG_KAIROS_TIMERS in the kairos controller's section of
cgroup-v2.rst: which timed waits of a latency-critical task get no
slack, that a task's own choice wins, what /proc/PID/timerslack_ns
shows, and when a relabel takes effect. Add "kairos.notimerclass" to
kernel-parameters.txt.

Signed-off-by: Aayush Nair <aayushnair204@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst         | 9 +++++++++
 Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst b/Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst
index c886bb547f83b0464a4d3597fc5d5b08b739c81c..7ce9b0213fdb31eb6247ccd278652e89caad43b0 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst
@@ -3014,6 +3014,15 @@ With cgroup writeback, writeback counts for the cgroup that dirtied the
 pages.  mq-deadline serves an idle request anyway once it has waited
 "prio_aging_expire".
 
+With the CONFIG_KAIROS_TIMERS config option the class also steers timer
+slack, unless "kairos.notimerclass" is on the kernel command line: the
+timed waits of a latency-critical task (sleeps, poll, select and epoll
+timeouts, futex waits, sigtimedwait, semtimedop, io_getevents) end on
+time, with no slack, as a realtime task's do.  A task which chose its own
+slack with prctl(PR_SET_TIMERSLACK) or /proc/PID/timerslack_ns keeps it,
+and that file shows the task's own slack either way.  The class is read
+when the wait begins, so a timer armed before a relabel keeps its slack.
+
 
 Non-normative information
 -------------------------
diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt b/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
index 6c77a0dec8483801b658e9a0f4eac5f837e7d7c2..c855417d4f4935206dcf8d0c92fcee10f7597201 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
@@ -2916,6 +2916,11 @@ Kernel parameters
 			(CONFIG_KAIROS_BOOT_SCHEDULER). Kairos's init reads
 			the same word and leaves the scheduler off too.
 
+	kairos.notimerclass
+			[KNL] Don't let Kairos task classes steer timer slack
+			(CONFIG_KAIROS_TIMERS): a latency-critical task's
+			timed waits get its usual slack.
+
 	kasan_multi_shot
 			[KNL] Enforce KASAN (Kernel Address Sanitizer) to print
 			report on every invalid memory access. Without this
